BT 1 0 0 1 0 333.804 Tm .7095 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: No. The divestiture order is invalid and must be set aside, and the Commission must instead) Tj T* 0 Tw .95 Tw (impose the equally effective supervised price and supply commitment that restores rivalry with) Tj T* 0 Tw (less intrusion.) Tj  T* 1.107692 Tw (Under R.A. No. 10667 Sec. 12\(d\) allowing stoppage or redress only upon substantial evidence) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.2 Tw (after due notice and hearing through injunctions, divestment and disgorgement, and Sec. 12\(h\)) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.371273 Tw (permitting adjustment or divestiture orders only where no equally effective behavioral remedy) Tj T* 0 Tw 5.403273 Tw (exists or where any equally effective behavioral remedy would be more burdensome,) Tj T* 0 Tw .553714 Tw (proportionate only to lasting or repeated infringement risk rooted in structure, as enforced by an) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.213846 Tw (independent enforcer under Tatad v. Secretary of DOE \(G.R. No. 124360, November 5, 1997\)) Tj T* 0 Tw .264857 Tw (pursuant to 1987 Constitution Art. XII Sec. 19, mere listing of divestiture among remedies never) Tj T* 0 Tw (makes it freely electable.) Tj  T* .7616 Tw (Here, the Commission found a cement cartel after due hearing but ordered members to sell two) Tj T* 0 Tw .056308 Tw (plants although it conceded a supervised price and supply commitment would restore rivalry, and) Tj T* 0 Tw .507429 Tw (the cartel wrongly reads mere listing of divestiture as free choice, but the admitted effectiveness) Tj T* 0 Tw .645231 Tw (of the behavioral commitment defeats the first statutory condition and shows the order punishes) Tj T* 0 Tw (structure rather than curing conduct proportionately.) Tj  T* 2.1744 Tw (The Commission therefore vacates divestiture, substitutes the effective behavioral order with) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.59 Tw (monitoring and retains disgorgement or fines if warranted, reserving divestiture for proof that) Tj T* 0 Tw (conduct relief cannot work or burdens more